      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Xavier%2C_Montana",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1887, Jesuit priests Urban Grassi and Peter Paul Prando erected a permanent mission church for the Crow people.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Xavier%2C_Montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "That mission’s school, now called Pretty Eagle School, remains affiliated with the Catholic church.",
